    "question": {
      ":question/id": "44a360a2-b057-5c61-bd96-a660b3dd8cb0",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n- \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y e^{- x} - 8 y^{2}=- 2 y\\,.\n$$\n\nAssume $y\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}- \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y e^{- x} - 8 y^{2}=- 2 y \\\\ - \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} y e^{- x} - 8 y^{2} + 2 y=0 \\\\ - y (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{- x} + 8 y - 2)=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{- x} + 8 y - 2=0 \\\\ e^{x}\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} e^{- x} + 8 y - 2\\right)=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 8 y e^{x} - 2 e^{x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(8 e^{x})}_{P(x)}y=\\underbrace{2 e^{x}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 8 y e^{x}=2 e^{x}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=8 e^{x}$ and $Q(x)=2 e^{x}.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
